        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0359" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg259"/>

                <head>No. 166.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 1, 1880</date>.
                        (Received June 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 673.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 665, in which
                    I stated that Mr. von Brandt had been charged by the diplomatic body with the
                    duty of preparing a scheme for the control of transit trade outwards, I have now
                    the honor to hand you herewith a copy of his memorandum and of the transit-pass
                    (outward) rules proposed by him and revised by the foreign representatives in
                    conference.</p>
                <p>Mr. von Brandt is to place this scheme before the Tsung-li Yamên on the part of
                    the diplomatic body.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEOEGE F. SEWAED.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d166-a1.xml" xpointer="d166-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d166-a2.xml" xpointer="d166-a2"/>
